== test: gh492-idle-kill ==
  workdir: /var/folders/69/3l_82qtj7fzglnt_jjg07jh40000gn/T//gh492-idle.al0X0m
  PASS: the sampler collected enough readings for a verdict (samples=3)
  PASS: a blocked turn accumulates idle time (idle=8.07783091600868s) — killable before the wall cap
  FAIL: CONTROL FAILED: a progressing turn reported idle=6.810299417003989s — this bound is trigger-happy and would kill good reviews
  PASS: blocked and progressing are separated by the signal the bound acts on (8.07783091600868s vs 6.810299417003989s)
  FAIL: expected timeout-idle-unknown for the blocked turn, got timeout-unclassified
  PASS: the progressing turn still classifies as timeout-slow-but-progressing — not conflated with idle
  PASS: idle_seconds() is None before any sample — callers must read that as 'do not kill'
  PASS: agy-turn guards the idle bound behind idle_cap > 0 (RELAY_TURN_IDLE_S=0 disables it)
  PASS: agy-turn treats an unmeasured idle reading as not-killable
  PASS: CONSULT: a hung advisor is seen as idle when scoped to its own pid (idle=3.0254180420015473s)
  PASS: CONSULT: the SHARED-parent scope masks that same hang (idle=0.4196225829946343s) — which is why root_pid exists
  PASS: a growing transcript FILE registers as progress (advisors share a worktree; a file is per-advisor)
  PASS: a missing transcript reads 0.0 rather than raising — an advisor that never writes is still measurable
  PASS: consult guards the idle bound (CONSULT_IDLE_S=0 restores pure wall-cap behaviour)
  PASS: consult treats an unmeasured idle reading as not-killable
  PASS: consult scopes each advisor's diagnostics to that advisor's own pid
  gh492-idle-kill: 14 pass, 2 fail
